meta {
  name: Confluence
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/adx/confluence?tickers=TQQQ,SQQQ&timeframes=M1,M5
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  tickers: TQQQ,SQQQ
  timeframes: M1,M5
  ~ticker: TQQQ
  ~period: 14
  ~threshold: 25
  ~rising: 3
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # ADX Confluence — high-confidence trend read
  
  Fuses multiple confirmations rather than trusting raw ADX alone. Read-only.
  Per ticker, on each requested timeframe (latest completed bar):
  - bias gated on strength (direction only when ADX >= threshold, else NEUTRAL),
  - DI spread and whether it is widening,
  - ADX slope (rising across the `rising` lookback),
  - ADXR (smoothed ADX rating).
  Then combines across timeframes + a volume-expansion check into a 0–N score
  and a verdict: STRONG_BULLISH / BULLISH / NEUTRAL / BEARISH / STRONG_BEARISH.
  
  ## Query
  - `ticker` / `tickers` — one or many; omit to screen the universe.txt pool.
  - `timeframes` — comma-separated (default M1,M5). All must agree for a STRONG verdict.
  - `period` / `threshold` / `rising` — optional overrides of webull.adx.*.
  
  ## Response (200)
  { verdict, score, volumeExpanding, timeframeAgreement,
    byTimeframe: [ { timeframe, adx, adxr, plusDi, minusDi, diSpread,
                     diWidening, adxRising, trending, bias, pattern } ],
    reason }
  (single explicit ticker returns just that object; multiple/universe returns a list
   sorted by score, highest first.)
}
